  "study_notes": {
    "observed": "Job Corps field survey photos (<=2018-09, pp.237/265). WSW side bound at medium from outer-489 (camera on the Avenue D sidewalk at the NW corner, looking SSE) and courtyard-489 (same pine and gate): the north wing's west end is a one-storey blank white stucco block; the 4.5 m slot between it and the west wing (footprint edges e1-e5) is a gated breezeway with an open stair; the west wing's WSW face is two-storey white stucco with pairs of windows, each under its own blue box hood, on both storeys. Courtyard-487 (camera SE of the courtyard looking NW) shows the north wing's courtyard face as a blank one-storey block with a tall louvre and steel flue stacks on the roof.",
    "inferred": "North wing one storey throughout (seen at its west end and courtyard face); the east wing keeps the Level 1 two storeys. Window-pair stations past the second pair, window and hood sizes, flue and louvre positions, the stair bay and door in the breezeway. Unbound sides are plain white stucco (owner rule) with one door per building: 487 on the 5th Street face, 489 in the breezeway.",
    "footprint": "Frozen ring split into five blocks: one-storey north wing (487) with its NE corner, two-storey east wing in two parts, two-storey west wing (489) with the link behind the breezeway."
  }
}
